msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:286
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Chat Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:288
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remove IP Address Logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:292
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the following command to remove all IP address records from closed chats "
"that haven't been updated in the last seven days:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:293
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Chat::Session.where(state: 'closed').where('updated_at < ?', "
"7.days.ago).each do |session|\n"
"next if session.preferences['remote_ip'].blank?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:297
#, no-wrap
msgid "session.preferences.delete('geo_ip')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "session.preferences.delete('remote_ip')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:303
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"session.save!(touch: false)\n"
"end\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/console.md:308
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Working on Zammad Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:312
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In this section, you can find some settings which you can set in the Zammad "
"UI as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:313
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket_hook Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:318
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This will give you the ticket hook that you'll find inside the `[]` in front "
"of the ticket number. By default this will be `Ticket#` - you shouldn't "
"change this setting in a productive system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:319
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ticket_hook')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:323
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "FQDN Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:326
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current FQDN setting of Zammad and, if needed, adjust it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:327
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This setting has no effect on SSL certificates or any web server\n"
"configurations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:333
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get current FQDN:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('fqdn')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:337
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set a new FQDN:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:337
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('fqdn', 'new.domain.tld')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:341
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP(s) Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:345
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This setting indirectly belongs to your FQDN setting and is relevant for "
"variable based URLs (e.g. in notifications) Zammad generated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:346
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This setting also affects Zammad's CSRF token behavior. If you set\n"
"this to e.g. HTTPs but you're using HTTP, logging in will\n"
"fail!\n"
"\n"
"It has no effect on SSL certificates or any web server configuration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:355
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current http type:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:355
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('http_type')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:359
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change the http type to HTTPs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:359
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('http_type', 'https')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/console.md:363
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Storage Provider Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:369
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The storage provider setting is set to `DB` on default installations.  "
"However, if you receive a lot of attachments or have a fairly busy "
"installation, using the database to store attachments is not the best "
"approach."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:371
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current attachment storage:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:371
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('storage_provider')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:375
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change attachment storage to database"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/console.md:375
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('storage_provider', 'DB')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:384
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have already stored files and want to move them, you can use the "
"following example. Please be aware that this operation should only be "
"executed in non-productive environments. In case you have to perform it in "
"production environments, you should specify a sleep delay - otherwise your "
"Zammad can be unresponsive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/console.md:386
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Move files from DB to File with a specified delay after each file in "
"seconds:"
