"token = '{zendesk token}'\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Update Zammad settings:\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_zendesk_endpoint', \"https://#{subdomain}/api/v2\")\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_zendesk_endpoint_username', email)\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_zendesk_endpoint_key', token)\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_backend', 'zendesk')\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_mode', true)\n"
"```\n"
"Check your configuration in a dry run:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"Sequencer.process('Import::Zendesk::ConnectionTest')\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Run the migration:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"job = ImportJob.create(name: 'Import::Zendesk')\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"AsyncImportJob.perform_later(job)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Webserver Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide is only relevant for package installations. During the "
"installation, Zammad tries to automatically install a configuration file to "
"your nginx.  You can find example configuration files for your webserver in "
"the ``contrib/`` directory of your Zammad installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case this out-of-the-box approach doesn't work for you, you can find some "
"hints for your configuration. You can use either Nginx or Apache 2 (only "
"referred to as Apache in the following text)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Get a SSL Certificate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You have to use a named configuration which is not configured by default. To "
"fix this, open the ``zammad.conf`` in your webserver's config directory and "
"replace the ``server_name localhost`` (Nginx) or ``ServerName localhost`` "
"(Apache)  with your Zammad domain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "The config directories are usually:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Nginx: ``/etc/nginx/conf.d/``, ``/etc/nginx/vhosts.d/``, "
"``/etc/nginx/sites-available/``"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Apache: ``/etc/apache2/conf.d/``, ``/etc/httpd/vhosts.d/``, "
"``/etc/apache2/sites-available/``"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's Encrypt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There are two common tools to get certificates, to which your find a basic "
"configuration below: [certbot](https://certbot.eff.org/instructions) and "
"[acme.sh](https://github.com/acmesh-official/acme.sh/wiki). Have a look at "
"their documentation for further configuration details and other examples."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"===certbot\n"
"\n"
"If not happened automatically, you have to install the nginx or apache "
"plugin\n"
"for certbot: ``python3-certbot-nginx`` or ``python3-certbot-apache``\n"
"\n"
"During the first certbot run it will request additional information once.\n"
"Replace ``<webserver>`` in below command by either ``apache``, ``httpd`` "
"or\n"
"``nginx`` to match your setup.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"certbot --<webserver> -d zammad.example.com\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Certbot will now attempt to issue a certificate for you. If successful,\n"
"certbot will ask you if you want to ``[1] not redirect`` or ``[2] "
"redirect``\n"
"automatically. You can choose to not redirect if you plan to use the "
"sample\n"
"configuration of Zammad.\n"
"\n"
"From now on, certbot will automatically renew your installed certificates "
"if\n"
"they’re valid for 30 days or less.\n"
"\n"
"===acme.sh\n"
"\n"
"Change the default certificate authority to Let's encrypt:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"acme.sh --set-default-ca  --server letsencrypt\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Issue your certificate and replace ``<webserver>`` in the following "
"command\n"
"with either ``apache`` or ``nginx`` or ``standalone`` for other webserver.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"acme.sh --issue --<webserver> -d zammad.example.com\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"It is not recommended to use the stored certificates directly. You should\n"
"install the certificate to a directory of your choice instead as you can "
"see\n"
"in the next command below. We’re using ``/etc/ssl/private/`` in this case,\n"
"but you can use any directory you like.\n"
"\n"
"Replace ``<webserver>`` with ``apache2``, ``httpd`` or ``nginx``.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"acme.sh --install-cert -d zammad.example.com \\\n"
"    --cert-file      /etc/ssl/private/zammad.example.com.pem  \\\n"
"    --key-file       /etc/ssl/private/zammad.example.com.key  \\\n"
"    --fullchain-file /etc/ssl/private/zammad.example.com.full.pem \\\n"
"    --reloadcmd     \"systemctl force-reload <webserver>\"\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"From now on, acme.sh will automatically renew your installed certificates "
"if\n"
"they’re valid for 30 days or less.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Commercial CA"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you prefer to use certificates from a different official Certificate "
"Authority (CA) than Let's Encrypt, you can do so as well. Just get your "
"certificate bundle, install it according to their documentation and continue "
"with adjusting the webserver configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:103
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adjusting the Webserver Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "Make sure to never use HTTP connections - we encourage you to use HTTPS!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:111
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1 - Get a Current Config File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:115
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Copy & overwrite the default ``zammad.conf``. Adjust your Nginx config "
"directory according to your setup:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:116
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cp /opt/zammad/contrib/nginx/zammad_ssl.conf "
"/etc/nginx/sites-available/zammad.conf\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:120
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2 - Adjust the Config File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:123
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:199
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Adjust the just copied file with a text editor of your choice (e.g. vi or "
"nano)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:126
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Locate any ``server_name`` directive and adjust ``example.com`` to the "
"domain of your Zammad instance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:129
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:205
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Now you'll need to adjust the path and file names for your ssl certificates "
"you obtained. Adjust the following directives to match your setup:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:133
#, markdown-text
msgid "``ssl_certificate`` (your ssl certificate)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:133
#, markdown-text
msgid "``ssl_certificate_key`` (the certificates private key)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:133
#, markdown-text
msgid "``ssl_trusted_certificate`` (the public CA certificate)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:137
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you don't have a ``dhparam.pem`` file yet, you can easily adapt the "
"example below to generate this file. You can find the correct path in your "
"webserver config. Search for ``ssl_dhparam``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:138
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:214
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"openssl dhparam -out <path>/dhparam.pem 4096\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:142
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3 - Adjust HTTPS Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:148
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:225
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Our default configuration aims for a broad support of end user devices. This "
"may not fit your needs. Mozilla has a great [ssl-config "
"generator](https://ssl-config.mozilla.org/) that should help you to meet "
"your requirements!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:149
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4 - Save & Reload"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:153
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Reload your nginx with ``systemctl reload nginx`` to apply your "
"configuration changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:156
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:268
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After that, you should be greeted by our getting started wizard.  Go on with "
"the [first steps in Zammad](/en/tutorials/first-steps)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:157
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Apache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:159
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1 - Enable Module"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:163
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad requires a module (``a2enmod``) which is not enabled by "
"default. CentOS users have to adjust a config file because this module is "
"not available there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:164
#, no-wrap
msgid "a2enmod proxy proxy_html proxy_http proxy_wstunnel headers ssl\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:167
#, no-wrap
msgid "systemctl restart apache2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details Config for CentOS)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:171
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Add/uncomment the appropriate ``LoadModule`` statements in your Apache "
"config\n"
"in ``/etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf``:\n"
"```\n"
"LoadModule headers_module modules/mod_headers.so\n"
"LoadModule proxy_module modules/mod_proxy.so\n"
"LoadModule proxy_html_module modules/mod_proxy_html.so\n"
"LoadModule proxy_http_module modules/mod_proxy_http.so\n"
"LoadModule proxy_wstunnel_module modules/mod_proxy_wstunnel.so\n"
"```\n"
"Restart your webserver after saving the configuration.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:185
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2 - Get a Current Config File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:189
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The package installation copied a ``zammad.conf`` file to your webserver "
"config directory. Check if it is present and do not rename this file!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:191
#, markdown-text
msgid "Adjust your Apache config directory according to your setup:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:192
#, no-wrap
msgid "ls /etc/apache2/sites-available\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:196
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3 - Adjust the Config File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:202
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Locate any ``ServerName`` directive and adjust ``example.com`` to the domain "
"of your Zammad instance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:209
#, markdown-text
msgid "``SSLCertificateFile`` (your ssl certificate)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:209
#, markdown-text
msgid "``SSLCertificateKeyFile``(the certificates private key)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:209
#, markdown-text
msgid "``SSLCertificateChainFile`` (the public CA certificate)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:213
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you don't have a ``dhparam.pem`` file yet, you can easily adapt the "
"example below to generate this file. You can find the correct path in your "
"webserver config. Search for ``SSLOpenSSLConfCmd DHParameters``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:219
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4 - Adjust HTTPS Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:226
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 5 - Enable the Site"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:230
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This step mostly depends on your selected folders and should only affect "
"``sites-available`` folders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Ubuntu, Debian, OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"Make sure the following line is present in your Apache config\n"
"(``/etc/apache2/apache2.conf``):\n"
"```\n"
"IncludeOptional sites-enabled/*.conf\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Enable it:\n"
"```bash\n"
"a2ensite zammad\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS\n"
"\n"
"Make sure the following line is present in your Apache config\n"
"(``/etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf``):\n"
"```\n"
"IncludeOptional sites-enabled/*.conf\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Enable it:\n"
"```bash\n"
"ln -s /etc/httpd/sites-available/zammad_ssl.conf /etc/httpd/sites-enabled/\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:261
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 6 - Save & Reload"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:265
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Reload your apache with ``systemctl reload apache2`` to apply your "
"configuration changes."
msgstr ""
